{"step_index":57,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T19:12:36Z","thinking":"UltraFusion's bandwidth is significantly higher, reaching 2,500 GB/s compared to Thunderbolt 4's 5 GB/s, representing a 500x difference. The UltraFusion architecture utilizes a high number of interconnect signals and low latency. This comparison highlights the substantial performance gap.\n\n\nThunderbolt's latency and bandwidth are orders of magnitude slower than on-package unified memory, making RAM sharing between Macs over Thunderbolt architecturally impossible. The initial query regarding RAM sharing is definitively answered; unified memory's design inherently precludes external pooling. Distributed computing support within specific Apple applications warrants further investigation to determine if it provides indirect resource utilization.\n\n\nDistributed processing capabilities across Apple platforms are being examined. Legacy features like Logic Node and Xgrid have been deprecated, suggesting a shift away from built-in distributed processing at the OS level. Remote access tools like macOS Screen Sharing, Apple Remote Desktop, and SSH provide alternative connectivity methods.\n\nThunderbolt Bridge creates a high-speed network for data transfer and workloads, but it doesn't pool memory; instead, it provides IP networking for tasks like file transfers and remote execution. Target Disk Mode allows mounting a Mac's drive on another.\n\n\nExamined \"Share Disk\" as a replacement for Target Disk Mode, confirming it provides network access to storage but not shared RAM or compute resources. Further research shows macOS Sequoia and later versions lack distributed shared memory functionality, with virtual memory management limited to local storage.\n\nAlthough macOS introduces Thunderbolt RDMA for specific AI frameworks, it does not support OS-level unified memory expansion or cross-Mac memory pooling.\n\n\nExamining the evolution of Apple's distributed computing solutions, Xgrid, a deprecated technology, utilized Bonjour for discovering compute nodes, highlighting a historical shift. Modern approaches have moved towards containerization, cloud, and specialized frameworks, with MLX emerging as a successor for Apple Silicon. Evaluating Universal Control, Sidecar, and AirPlay, no resource sharing occurs; each device operates independently, and Sidecar uses the Mac's resources, ruling out unified memory.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"Logic Node\" Apple deprecated OR removed Logic Pro","toolAction":"Searching the web","toolSummary":"Search Logic Node deprecation in Logic Pro"}}]}
{"step_index":58,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T19:12:46Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-20T00:42:46+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-20T00:42:49+05:30\nThe search for \"\"Logic Node\" Apple deprecated OR removed Logic Pro\" returned the following summary:\nLogic Node, the feature that allowed users to distribute audio processing across multiple networked Mac computers, has been **discontinued**[1][2].\n\nIt was effectively removed from Logic Pro when the application moved past the era of Logic Pro 9[2]. The technology is no longer a part of the modern Logic Pro workflow[1][2].\n\n### Important Distinction\nPlease be careful not to confuse the discontinued \"Logic Node\" (the networking feature) with **automation nodes**[3]. Automation nodes are the points you place on automation curves to adjust volume, pan, or effects parameters over time[3]; these remain a core, active part of Logic Pro and are frequently discussed in user forums[4].\n\nSources:\n[1] [logicprohelp.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEv6jD7H2h2mOEU8rBUoR8JkT71zdKreLZeBWqOyR810i4sGdU09La9zfY4vG_u1GlRYbsuolYtqeqreDv1_-Fgv33Mpbaj_NeLIptaxONLLK6X6TFJ6Ye6x4ejx-EAdNaEHyQ3tCjv8DVq2EQZAr1uAxc5mGdAItg=)\n[2] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHNgNzDjOcRCziu-Z3uqlIC48nHoSQ2XXIBP2zomsViNiKSJ0-hLYJzkjoOBThfk34fWEhpJSjMahx5nt8egRxW3RkqWUv-G9m_Ag7hkWJdul1-AO6xMjApsaAc8eGBxxmQV_aTV3CgXUoXOPeFNsCR694oYaJUd5sYCuskhHKcZrdeY2nXCs3kSmdRv1dafaS-Mj1K1SL3FI8xgeRnXy-GLWo=)\n[3] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFy8aqvdbnv2eO_BSUQeoc2B_hNK0erei3O4oro3zXfM-KF6kfuKIOB3oSmXhTQReQopBCNJcPA7XJXHttRWM1hYiKpETB3WtkHzxqedY4hG4J4iJzPDV5sN00wnUHfDqZ9)\n[4] [facebook.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFAX3D_9toqcnFR6m2e-4RTfbjMFR8iLebd8rgGtkjfZCg79ITAj9bjgmmDOWejulioM7p6YqI_mXapAfi7RF7FD0AqngKif9nldiq7QGi_4IbuMYxCsM2VMEQ9v